WEBVTT

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.030
Delunio attacked Natra,

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.950
and now Soljest is coming to
Delunio's aid because they're allies.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.490
That's the pretext.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:44.160
However, it is only Soljest's army
that is invading Natra.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.290
No doubt Delunio is hoping Soljest
and Natra will wear each other down.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.920
"Soljest"     "Natra"
"Delunio"

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.920
No doubt Delunio is hoping Soljest
and Natra will wear each other down.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.960
"Soljest"     "Natra"

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.960
"Delunio"

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.350
War is such a tedious matter.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.560
I was sure that prince had
a trick up his sleeve, but...

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.900
I bring urgent news!
Our scouts spotted the Natran army!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.940
They number seven to eight thousand,
but there's no sign of the prince!

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.070
Seeking reconciliation with Delunio
<i>is </i>a clever move to halt our army.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.410
But Sirgis won't be swayed.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:25.370
It seems I won't get
to face the prince in battle.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.130
An ambush?

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.670
I will claim your head!

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:44.310
Marvelous! Now <i>this </i>is a battle!

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.950
I live for the clash of arms!

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.450
Can we win the war?

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.490
I don't know.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.910
But the opponent we must face now is...

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.290
What a pleasant surprise.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:14.000
It is an honor to have such esteemed
personages visit our kingdom.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.510
We're grateful that you would see us
on such short notice, Sir Sirgis.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.050
Think nothing of it.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.810
Turnabout is fair play,
for I have now barged in on you.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:02.780
War broke out between the Marden region
and your kingdom over territorial claims.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:09.120
We are here to see whether there might be
a peaceful resolution to this matter.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.960
I see.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:17.210
This territorial dispute is an
unfortunate misunderstanding.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:21.050
That is my view,
and I believe there is room to talk.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.010
Now this is odd.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:27.220
When we sought the legitimate
return of land we lent you,

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.430
was it not <i>you </i>who refused to talk?

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:36.690
And regarding the territorial issue,
Delunio resolved the matter as we saw fit.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.150
You did?

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:43.030
After the Soljester army retakes
the land Delunio loaned to Marden,

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:47.030
we arranged for them to return it to us.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:52.080
As such, there is no need for me
to negotiate with you, Lady Zenovia.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.330
Delunio and Soljest's ties
are stronger than I thought.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.540
But I must find a way to pull them apart.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:03.170
Because of me,
both Natra and Marden will suffer.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.850
I understand what you're saying.

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.980
But I wonder if it will
truly work out that well?

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.900
Are you suggesting
Natra will defeat Soljest?

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.690
That will never happen.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.230
That's precisely what you
should be concerned about!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.990
Soljest has a mighty army.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.450
That means they will
likely suffer little damage,

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:31.660
and their influence will only
keep growing once they win.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:36.460
Delunio must wish to avoid
the future I'm alluding to.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.710
If so, I will have to--

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:42.170
That is certainly worth some thought.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:46.470
However, Soljest has promised
to return our land once they take it.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.340
That can't be ignored.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.300
Now's my chance!

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:55.180
We shall surrender to Delunio
land twice the size of what you lent us!

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:59.560
That was a bold decision, Zenovia.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:03.530
Loss of land will harm your economy
and your military might.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:05.530
Plus, support among your people

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.490
and Marden's standing
within Natra will also suffer.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.320
But right now...

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.080
I must rob Soljest of just cause
and thereby halt the invasion.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.870
That is the most pressing matter.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:19.580
And I must make a sacrifice
to make it happen!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:27.130
It seems I must ask you to leave,
Marchioness Zenovia.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:32.970
There is nothing you could propose
that would make me change my mind.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.270
I have failed.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.890
No matter how she clamors,

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:41.270
Soljest will win a decisive victory,
and we will regain our land.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.730
Once I donate that land
to the Levetian faith,

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.940
I will surely be named to the Holy Elites!

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.530
With our venerable land,

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:52.660
devout and goodly people,
and traditional culture,

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.950
Delunio is already the guiding
light of the continent.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:02.670
And if I were to lead it as a Holy Elite,
our great kingdom would be unassailable.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.750
The future is looking bright.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.380
Sir Sirgis, I think it's time
we discuss why I'm really here.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.090
And that would be?

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:17.020
What do you say we
go kill Gruyere right now?

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.350
What?!

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:29.530
The Natrans have entered a
defensive formation and won't budge.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:33.410
That ambush got me
all excited for nothing.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:37.040
It won't be long before my officers
and their men grow impatient.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.870
If the Natrans continue
this tedious tactic tomorrow,

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.370
we will crush them
with a full-frontal assault.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.630
I have a report!

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.590
The Natrans are on the move!

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.840
They abandoned their camp
and are retreating!

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.840
The Natrans have been cowed!

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.800
Our exalted king has claimed
victory on the battlefield!

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.640
We are victorious!

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.690
Go kill King Gruyere with you?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.770
Why would I ever agree to such a proposal?

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:10.780
As Lady Zenovia said,
Soljest is growing ever more powerful.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.110
And that is precisely what I feared.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:17.410
If left unchecked, how many innocent
lives will the coming wars claim,

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:19.330
and how many will be displaced?

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.500
It pains my heart just thinking about it.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:27.340
I see. Your proposal was made out
of concern for your people?

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.710
That I can understand.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:34.430
Unfortunately, we cannot join you
in your fight against Soljest.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:39.640
But I am willing to accept those
who flee your land as refugees.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.970
You're too kind!

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.270
We all share the same continent.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:47.980
It is heartless to refuse sanctuary
to those caught in the maelstrom of war.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.820
Then I shall accept your kind proposal.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.740
The Kingdom of Natra will be
sending 800,000 refugees your way!

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.070
E-Eight hundred thousand?

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:02.250
As you said, Soljest has a mighty army.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:07.130
Our forces will be routed by their
superior numbers and tactics,

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.000
and the Kingdom of Natra
will undoubtedly fall.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:15.050
Policymakers must consider the security
of their people in such situations.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.850
I must find a safe haven for them.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:20.560
It's as simple as that.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:25.350
We could accept hundreds, even thousands,
but you want us to take 800,000?!

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.980
Our kingdom is not prepared
for such numbers!

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.860
That's what I thought.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.980
But I'm still going to send them.

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:36.990
If you were to do such a thing,
we'd use military force to stem the flow!

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:39.660
We will show no mercy and no quarter!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:45.080
Tens of thousands of Natrans will die
without ever reaching our kingdom!

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.170
Is that what you want?

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.330
You'll stop them by military force?

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.000
Is your army even capable of that?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:52.960
What?!

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.970
Doesn't the color yellow really stand out?

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.470
Yellow? What are you talking about?

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:02.680
Are you referring to that
current trend in our kingdom?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:06.690
That yellow dye is made
from a poisonous flower.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:07.730
Huh?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:12.570
It's so poisonous that when
you wear clothing dyed with it,

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:17.530
it slowly works its way into you,
weakening your body until you finally die.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.570
I don't believe such
an expedient toxin exists!

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:25.080
People will wonder
whether it's a plague or a curse.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.370
Delunians will start dying left
and right in the prime of their life.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:32.590
In their confusion,
people will spread baseless rumors.

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.510
More and more will seek
to flee the kingdom.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.340
The military will be
hard put to stop them.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:41.640
That's when I'll unleash
800,000 Natrans upon you!

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:45.890
Food and supplies will run short,
and your cities will cease to function.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:50.100
Your existing culture will be transformed,
and the impoverished Delunians

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:53.060
will seek to expel the Natran interlopers.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.320
Of course, the Natrans will resist,

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:59.700
and order will break down
as violence erupts across the land.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.820
Your army will be even harder pressed.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:05.700
In the meantime,
the neighboring kingdoms will

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.620
use your mistreatment of
our refugees as a pretext to invade.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:14.040
And then, oh my.
Stick a fork in Delunio. It's done.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:20.300
As if. Like you already said,
such an expedient toxin doesn't exist.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:24.760
But it's a rather troubling bluff,
isn't it, Sirgis?

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.720
He really is a monster.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:33.560
He's threatening to sacrifice
his kingdom to destroy his enemy.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:38.940
How does one born of royalty
concoct such a diabolical idea?

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:42.360
No one could pull off
such a preposterous scheme!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:47.990
How could you possibly get
800,000 Natrans to descend on Delunio?!

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:50.330
I did it with 30,000.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:56.170
That's right. He did it once in Mealtars.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:00.340
But 800,000 is an entirely
different thing than 30,000!

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:03.260
But even with that vast difference...

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:06.100
I should claim your head right here!

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:11.140
My little sister, Falanya, led the
30,000 Mealtarians. I simply helped.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:17.320
I left instructions to immediately unleash
the Natran hordes if I should die here.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.070
So what will it be?

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.280
I beg your pardon, sir!

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.660
We received word of the battle.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:29.660
Natra's army has been routed
after clashing with Soljest!

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:33.670
Wow, Soljest's army is impressive.
There's no stopping them.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:39.210
It won't be long before
they're at the gates of our capital.

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.670
I want details! Now!

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:46.090
W-We do not know much more,
except that Soljest is in pursuit!

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.640
Then find out more!

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:51.390
Yes, sir!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:59.980
General Hagal! Lady Ninym!

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.110
Are you all right?

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:03.490
This is nothing for me.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:04.740
Don't push your luck.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:08.740
At any rate, I'm pleased
you were able to make it back.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:12.700
His Highness's ambush plan
worked like a charm.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.420
But I am ashamed to report
we failed to slay the king.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:18.290
Pay it no mind.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:23.420
It is no easy task to take down
such big game in a single strike.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:27.760
Has the Soljester army realized
His Highness's true objective?

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.600
They can't possibly have.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.260
For his idea is far removed

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:35.350
from even the wildest imagination
of a warrior seeking victory.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:37.480
Detailed communication between

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:42.190
the homeland and the
battlefield is quite difficult.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:44.780
It takes time for news to travel,

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:50.450
and there is a predilection for reporting
the best news possible from the front.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:55.460
That is why despite both sides
taking light losses and falling back,

00:13:55.460 --> 00:14:00.040
the first report will be that the
Natran army has been routed.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:05.670
My brother mapped it all out
before going to Delunio, didn't he?

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.880
That's right.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.760
The speed of the Soljester
and Natran armies' advance.

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:12.890
The day, time, and location of the battle.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.970
The distance to Delunio's capital,

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:19.020
the time a swift steed would take
to arrive, and the diplomacy schedule.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:23.150
He took all that into account to
ensure the first report would arrive

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:26.070
while he was negotiating with Sir Sirgis.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:30.780
Can you really time your army's retreat
so it happens during negotiations?

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:33.080
It usually is impossible.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:38.160
However, the prince regent
is an exception to the rule.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.790
Now that's what I call perfect timing!

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.800
I can't believe the report
came just when I needed it!

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.220
This I will not abide!
You call this a negotiation?!

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.470
Do you think nothing of your people?!

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:53.680
I trust and treasure them, of course.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.640
No matter where they go,

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:58.440
I've no doubt they have
the strength to forge a new future.

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.480
That is what my people do.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.150
It's not possible.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.320
What sort of prince regent

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:09.820
gets his own people mixed up in
pulling off such a diabolical scheme?

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.820
It's not possible! It's just not--

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.490
I could.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:15.910
Y-You could?

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:21.120
He could? Knowing him, maybe it's true.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.380
Say it! Let me hear you say
there is no way you could do that.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.920
I'm going to join the Holy Elites!

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:30.340
I shall lead this kingdom and its people!

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.930
I will not lose like this!

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:36.680
By the way, I have
an antidote at the ready.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:40.060
Did he just say there's an antidote?

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:42.600
With that, the people would be...

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:48.360
My beloved people of
Delunio would be saved.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:55.580
The Natran army has likely
regrouped after its initial retreat

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:58.540
and is now battling Soljest once again.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:02.790
I'd like the Delunian army
to strike from the rear.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.010
That retreat was just a feint.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:18.810
We were shocked to find they had joined
another force in a fortified position.

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:27.520
They still have troops up above.

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:31.570
We are the army of Soljest!
We have nothing to fear!

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.370
How boring.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:41.620
They've broken through our first
and second lines of defense.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.170
We cannot reform our lines
with our dwindling numbers.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:48.710
It's only a matter of time
before our fortress falls.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.800
No, that may not happen after all.

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:09.150
It seems we were in time.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:16.910
Attention, all troops!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.200
We have a new enemy from the southwest!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.450
That is... They're flying
the Delunian banner!

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:25.420
The Natrans are making
a sortie from their fort!

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:27.630
The front line requests reinforcements!

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:30.800
Delunio and Natra are acting in concert!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.050
A magnificent move, Prince of Natra!

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.760
You got Delunio to turn!

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.470
Majesty! We will be caught
in a pincer move!

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:43.520
Luckily, there is no enemy movement
to the north! There's still time to flee!

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:46.600
Flee?! Are you mad?!

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:48.650
We'll smash through the Delunian lines!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.650
All troops!

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:52.940
With me!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:57.780
If we can cut our way
through the Delunians,

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:01.370
they will serve as a wall that
will block the Natran onslaught.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.200
When they come together,

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.670
they'll be thrown into chaos
and won't recover for some time.

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:12.420
Meanwhile, we will wheel about
and slay the leaders of both armies!

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.300
Got ya.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:34.650
This may seem rude.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:37.320
No need for manners here!

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:52.130
His Majesty... the King.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.570
Forgive the intrusion.

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:23.450
What the...?! King Gruyere?

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:25.620
Or am I mistaken?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.910
The young prince. It's been a while!

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.880
You've changed quite a bit
since I last saw you.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.800
You mean this scrawny body?

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:37.880
With my metabolism,

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:43.390
I shed weight like no tomorrow
in times of injury or overexertion.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:45.390
Now, why are you here?

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:47.640
Has the date of my execution been set?

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:50.440
No, I have no intention of executing you.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:54.560
We ended up exchanging blows,
but we were just victims of circumstance.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:59.490
I still wish to forge friendly ties
with the Kingdom of Soljest.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:05.490
Yes, but isn't executing me
the only way to appease Delunio?

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:07.910
That's not the case.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:13.210
Execution is off the table in the talks
I plan to hold between our three kingdoms.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:14.750
That is unexpected.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:18.340
But I imagine Sirgis
will be vehemently opposed.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:20.760
He was brought down.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.720
Sir Sirgis basically took it upon himself
to forge an alliance with Soljest.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:28.430
But then he scuttled it
and joined forces with Natra.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:32.140
That ended up costing the great
and powerful Sir Sirgis

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.270
his political career.

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:38.320
Now I see. Natra doesn't want a war
with the Levetian religion.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.570
And Soljest would like
to avert my execution.

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:45.030
So our kingdoms managed
to quietly bring Sirgis down.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:48.830
Now, if you would please sign these.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:52.540
Then you may return home
with the group summoned from Soljest.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.380
No, I think I will die here.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.250
What?!

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:00.670
I live my life the way I want.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.340
I won't have my life spared
by other people's gambles.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:08.010
Please wait a moment. That would mean...

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:11.020
All-out war between Natra
and the Levetian religion.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:13.850
Now you're in a real pickle, aren't you?

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.150
But I'll be dead, so what do I care?

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:22.110
He'd sacrifice his life in a last-ditch
effort to gain the upper hand?

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.780
What a dirty move!

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:27.490
I'll agree to return home in
one piece under one condition.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:29.370
And that would be?

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.660
Tell me the true nature
of the beast within you.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:34.830
The beast inside me?

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:38.290
Everyone has a beast within.

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:40.880
Call it desire if you like.

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:46.010
I want to know what your inner
beast feeds on. What does it want?

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:51.850
Tell me that, and your three-kingdom
talks will proceed as you wish.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:03.820
Are you... serious?

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:06.450
You're free to believe what you will.

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:08.410
But one thing is sure.

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:10.700
If you die here, King Gruyere,

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:16.120
you'll never know if
I truly meant what I just said.

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:23.590
Nice move! I surrender!

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:27.880
I can't die without hearing
the truth of the matter!

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:30.300
I'm looking forward to it!

00:22:30.300 --> 00:22:32.560
We'll see.

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:38.440
I'm not the only one eager to see
where your inner beast takes you.

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:44.070
Let's see how far you make it
through this chaotic continent!

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:47.320
I'll be watching with great interest,

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:53.450
young prince, Wein Salema Arbalest!

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:57.830
Another all-nighter.

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:03.130
Morning, Ninym.

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:05.510
Good morning, Wein.

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:10.220
The financial report is ready.

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:11.510
Are we in the green?

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:12.430
It's a toss-up.

00:23:12.430 --> 00:23:15.560
The reparations we imposed
covered the cost of the war.

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:18.520
And the operation to bring down Sirgis

00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:22.360
and buy back the surrendered
land wasn't all that costly.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:26.990
But the conflict you had with Gruyere
will cost us since he is a Holy Elite.

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:30.280
The Levitians are giving
Natra the cold shoulder.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:33.620
Far fewer pilgrims pass
through Marden these days,

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:36.080
so trade there has nosedived.

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:41.120
At least that will keep Marden
from growing too big for their britches.

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:45.130
W-Wait! What about the
unprecedented boom times for Natra?!

00:23:45.130 --> 00:23:46.420
The bubble burst.

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:49.720
What about milking
my position for all it's worth?

00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:52.720
I won't be living the good life anymore?!

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:54.470
Kiss it goodbye.

00:23:56.890 --> 00:23:58.600
Snapped out of it yet?

00:23:58.600 --> 00:24:01.310
Then let's get to work.

00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:09.400
I <i>really </i>can't wait to sell
this kingdom and disappear!
